## Final Judgement
### Summary of Key Insights
The retrieved evidence clearly demonstrates that the claim "New Zealand’s new Food Bill bans gardening" is an online hoax. The legislation in question, officially known as the Food Act 2014 (which was introduced as Food Bill 160-2), contains absolutely no provisions that ban or restrict private, non-commercial home gardening, seed saving, or the sharing of homegrown food. A spokesperson for New Zealand's Ministry for Primary Industries confirmed that the Act only applies to food sold commercially and has no jurisdiction over personal gardens. The rumor originally stemmed from alarmist misinterpretations of the bill in 2011 and was subsequently kept alive as a long-running satirical joke on Reddit. Because the evidence is definitive and leaves no room for ambiguity, no further investigation is required.

